WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:05.833
One summer day a fox was trotting through the woods.

2
00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.631
He stopped to wipe his forehead.

3
00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:10.702
"Phew!" he thought.

4
00:00:10.703 --> 00:00:15.457
"It's quite hot today. I'm getting really thirsty."

5
00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:18.843
Just then the fox spotted a grapevine.

6
00:00:18.844 --> 00:00:22.567
It was wrapped around the trunk and branches of a tree.

7
00:00:22.568 --> 00:00:26.968
Hanging from a high branch was a bunch of sweet grapes.

8
00:00:26.969 --> 00:00:32.087
The fox loved all fruits, but sweet grapes were his favorite.

9
00:00:32.088 --> 00:00:34.886
And they were hanging right above his head!

10
00:00:34.887 --> 00:00:38.880
"Mmm." The fox licked his lips.

11
00:00:38.881 --> 00:00:44.662
"Those sweet grapes look quite juicy. I will get some!"

12
00:00:44.663 --> 00:00:49.136
The thirsty fox leaped up, ready to bite into those grapes.

13
00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:52.137
But the branch was much higher than he thought.

14
00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:55.830
His jaws snapped shut on nothing but air.

15
00:00:55.831 --> 00:01:01.079
The poor fox fell back down and tumbled on the ground.

16
00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.072
"Hmph!" The fox got up and dusted off his fur.

17
00:01:05.073 --> 00:01:07.986
"That's okay. I'll just try again!"

18
00:01:07.987 --> 00:01:11.462
The fox backed away from the tree to take a running leap.

19
00:01:11.463 --> 00:01:16.259
This time he jumped higher, but—

20
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.395
"Oof!" He tumbled onto the ground again.

21
00:01:20.396 --> 00:01:24.145
"Grr!" The fox gritted his teeth.

22
00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:27.344
"I must reach that branch!"

23
00:01:27.345 --> 00:01:28.883
He ran faster.

24
00:01:28.884 --> 00:01:30.455
He leaped higher.

25
00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.975
He tried again and again to get the grapes.

26
00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:37.160
But still he could not reach them.

27
00:01:37.161 --> 00:01:42.146
"Hmm." The fox scratched his head and stared at the fruit.

28
00:01:42.147 --> 00:01:46.575
"I really want those grapes. What can I do?"

29
00:01:46.576 --> 00:01:49.644
An owl was watching the fox from a nearby tree.

30
00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:52.509
So was a young gray squirrel.

31
00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:56.199
"Too bad, Fox," the owl called.

32
00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.152
"It looks like those sweet grapes are out of your reach."

33
00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:05.408
The squirrel nodded. "You'll never be able to get them, Fox.

34
00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:10.438
You can't climb like me. And you can't fly like Owl."

35
00:02:10.439 --> 00:02:14.845
The fox flushed. "How embarrassing!" he thought.

36
00:02:14.846 --> 00:02:18.620
He pretended to stare harder at the grapes above his head.

37
00:02:18.621 --> 00:02:24.632
"Oh!" The fox laughed as he tapped himself lightly on the head.

38
00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:27.772
"Silly me! I just realized something.

39
00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:31.721
Those aren't sweet grapes—they're sour ones.

40
00:02:31.722 --> 00:02:33.898
I dislike sour grapes.

41
00:02:33.899 --> 00:02:37.815
So, I won't waste one more minute of my time. Good-bye!"

42
00:02:37.816 --> 00:02:41.210
With a wave, the thirsty fox ran off.

43
00:02:41.211 --> 00:02:44.012
The young squirrel scratched his head.

44
00:02:44.013 --> 00:02:48.855
"Owl, why did the fox call them sour grapes?" the squirrel asked.

45
00:02:48.856 --> 00:02:50.441
"They're not sour.

46
00:02:50.442 --> 00:02:55.003
They're sweet—probably the sweetest grapes in the whole woods."

47
00:02:55.004 --> 00:03:00.031
The owl sighed. "It's simple, Squirrel.

48
00:03:00.032 --> 00:03:10.899
We often pretend to dislike the things that we can't have."

